# Ignore everything at the repo root by default
/*

# Whitelist directories and files we actually want tracked.
#
# Note: ``examples/`` is intentionally NOT whitelisted. Everything under
# ``examples/`` is project-internal — trainer templates assuming a
# specific RL framework (SB3 / sb3-contrib / OmniSafe), shell wrappers
# pinning algorithm + hparams + seed, paper-writing analysis tools, and
# rendering helpers tied to the SB3 zip checkpoint format. The public
# benchmark surface is the registered env id (``OmniPiano-*-v0``), the
# reward formulas, and the wrapper stack — NOT a particular way to
# train it. Users adopting OmniPiano are expected to wire their own
# trainer (RLlib, CleanRL, Mava, or SB3 — their choice) using the
# minimal ``omnipiano.make(env_id)`` snippet shown in the README.
!/omnipiano/
!/demos/
!/setup.py
!/README.md
!/action_index_reference.md

# Paper drafts co-evolve with the code (claims/abstract/sections in git)
!/paper/

# examples/: track DIRECT files (trainer templates / helper scripts) so the
# omnipiano.make() call sites stay version-controlled, but keep the subfolders
# ignored (logs/, runs/, figures_aggregate/, repertoire/, __pycache__/ are
# local run artifacts, not source). Subfolder tracking is opt-in per request.
!/examples/
/examples/*/

# Python bytecode cache (any __pycache__/ anywhere in the tree)
__pycache__/

# PIG dataset preprocessing artifacts (users run `robopianist preprocess` to generate)
omnipiano/envs/robopianist/music/data/pig_single_finger/

# Whitelist .gitignore itself
!.gitignore
